usageError.printed: no false case. printed is set only at hermes.go:62-63, after fs.Parse returns an error other than ErrHelp. In Go 1.26.6 every such error comes from failf, which prints the message and the usage to fs.Output(). That is stderr, because hermesSetup never calls SetOutput. ErrHelp returns nil. Every other error is printed once by main (main.go:41-54).

